    answer: "Omega-7 (palmitoleic acid) is a monounsaturated fatty acid found in a handful of plant foods, most notably the Himalayan sea-buckthorn berry. Most Indian diets get plenty of Omega-6 from cooking oils and some Omega-3 from flaxseed or walnut, but Omega-7 is far less common. Sea buckthorn is a whole-food plant supplement that can add this uncommon fatty acid to a daily plant-based diet. It is a food supplement, not a medicine."
  },
  {
    question: "How many Sujata Himalayan Sea Buckthorn capsules should I take per day?",
    answer: "A sensible daily serving is 1-2 capsules (650-1,300 mg) taken with food. For example: 1 capsule after breakfast and 1 after dinner with warm water. The fats in a normal meal help absorption of the fat-soluble carotenoids and Omega-7. Do not exceed 2 capsules per day without physician guidance. Children, pregnant and lactating women, and anyone on prescribed medicine should speak with their doctor before use."
  },
  {
    question: "Capsule or oil — which format is practical for daily use?",
    answer: "Sujata offers cold-pressed whole-berry extract in capsule form. Capsules give you a fixed, consistent 650 mg serving per piece, are easy to carry, do not leave a taste in the mouth and shield the Omega-7 from light. Bulk oil can lose freshness after opening because fatty acids oxidise on exposure to air and heat. The cold-pressed <40 °C capsule preserves the whole-berry nutrient matrix."
  },
  {
    question: "Can I take sea buckthorn with other food supplements or prescribed medicines?",
    answer: "Sujata Himalayan Sea Buckthorn is widely combined with Sujata Spirulina as a daily plant-based pairing (see the Spirulina + Sea Buckthorn combo pack). If you are on any prescribed medicine — blood thinners, blood-pressure or any long-term treatment — speak with your treating physician before starting any supplement. Supplements are additions to a diet, never substitutes for medical care."
  },
  {
    question: "How long should a daily sea buckthorn routine run before I review it?",
    answer: "Whole-food supplements build nutrition slowly over weeks and months — different from medicines that act in hours. A sensible personal review window is 90 days of daily, consistent use, followed by a self-check on how you feel and how your overall routine (diet, hydration, screen breaks, sleep) is going. There are no promised outcomes; individual experience varies with the rest of your lifestyle."
  },
  {
    question: "Are there side effects I should know about?",
    answer: "Sujata Himalayan Sea Buckthorn is a food supplement with a very benign profile in healthy adults at the 1-2 capsule daily serving. A few customers report mild loose stool in the first 3-5 days as the gut adapts to the fatty acids — usually resolves on its own. The natural carotenoids may slightly tint urine orange (harmless). Stop the supplement 2 weeks before any surgery. Discontinue and consult a doctor if any unusual reaction appears."
  },
  {
    question: "Is sea buckthorn a cure for any eye or dry-skin condition?",
    answer: "No. Sujata Himalayan Sea Buckthorn is a food supplement. It is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any eye condition, skin condition or any other disease. For diagnosed conditions such as dry-eye disease, speak with your ophthalmologist and follow the plan they prescribe. A food supplement can sit alongside that plan with their guidance."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the price of a 3-month supply?",
    answer: "Sujata Himalayan Sea Buckthorn Capsules (60 × 650 mg) are ₹649 for one month (≈ ₹21/day). For a 90-day supply, the Spirulina + Himalayan Sea Buckthorn 2-month combo pack is ₹1,100 (≈ ₹18/day) and ships with 2 free SpiruGlow soaps. Free Cash on Delivery pan-India via WhatsApp (+91 98347 83503). Refund policy: see /refund-policy."
  }
];

// Clean Article schema — no MedicalWebPage, no MedicalCondition, no Keratoconjunctivitis reference.
const articleSchema = [
  {
    "@type": "Article",
    "@id": `${pageUrl}/#article`,
    "headline": "Himalayan Sea Buckthorn Omega-7: Daily Nutrient for Natural Moisture & Comfort",
    "description": pageDescription,
    "image": "https://www.sujatanutrilive.com/products/sujata-sea-buckthorn-capsules-bottle-transparent.png",
    "inLanguage": "en-IN",
    "mainEntityOfPage": pageUrl,
    "datePublished": "2026-03-01T09:00:00+05:30",
    "dateModified": new Date().toISOString(),
    "author": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Sujata Nutrilive Nutrition Research Team",
      "url": "https://www.sujatanutrilive.com"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": BRAND_CONFIG.brandName,
      "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://www.sujatanutrilive.com/sujata-logo-transparent.png" }
    },
    "about": {
      "@type": "DietarySupplement",
      "name": "Sea Buckthorn (Hippophae rhamnoides)",
      "activeIngredient": "Palmitoleic acid (Omega-7), Vitamin C, Vitamin E, Beta-carotene, Flavonoids, 190+ phytonutrients",
      "sameAs": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippophae"
    }
  },
  {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "@id": `${pageUrl}/#faq`,
    "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": f.question,
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.answer }
    }))
  },
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "@id": `${pageUrl}/#breadcrumb`,
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.sujatanutrilive.com" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Learn", "item": "https://www.sujatanutrilive.com/science" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Himalayan Sea Buckthorn Omega-7", "item": pageUrl }
    ]
  }
];
---

<StoreLayout
